hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24018","Narrated to us Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us my father, from Ibn Ishaq, narrated to me al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Saad ibn Muadh, brother of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, from Mahmud ibn Labid, brother of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, he said: When Abu al-Haysar Anas ibn Rafi came to Mecca, and with him were youths of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, among them Iyas ibn Muadh, seeking an alliance from Quraysh against their people of the Khazraj, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard of them, so he came to them and sat with them and said to them: Do you want better than what you came for? They said: And what is that? He said: I am the Messenger of Allah, He sent me to the servants, I call them to worship Allah, not associating anything with Him, and a Book was revealed to me. Then he mentioned Islam and recited the Quran to them. So Iyas ibn Muadh, and he was a young boy, said: O people, this, by Allah, is better than what you came for. He said: So Abu Julays Anas ibn Rafi took a handful of the dust of al-Batha and struck it in the face of Iyas ibn Muadh. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up from them. And they left to Medina, and the battle of Buath occurred between al-Aws and al-Khazraj. He said: Then Iyas ibn Muadh did not live long before he died. Mahmud ibn Labid said: Those of my people who were present with him at his death informed me that they kept hearing him declare Allah One and magnify Him and praise Him and glorify Him until he died. So they had no doubt that he had died a Muslim. He had felt Islam in that sitting when he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he heard."
"24019","Narrated to us Bahz, narrated to me Ibrahim ibn Saad, narrated to us Ibn Shihab, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, and he had retained a mouthful that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had spat in his face from a bucket from a well of theirs."
"24020","Narrated to us Yazid, narrated to us Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, he said: One who saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the stones of oil narrated to me, supplicating thus, and he pointed with the insides of his palms toward his face."
"24021","Narrated to us Abu Said, narrated to us Sulayman, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, protects His believing servant from the world while He protects him, as you protect your sick from food and drink, fearing it for him."
"24022","And with this chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves a people, He tries them. So whoever is patient, for him is patience, and whoever panics, for him is panic."
"24023","Narrated to us Yaqub, narrated to us my father, from Ibn Ishaq, narrated to me Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah al-Ansari, from Mahmud ibn Labid, brother of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and prayed Maghrib with us in our mosque. When he finished it he said: Pray these two rakahs in your houses, as supererogatory after Maghrib."
"24024","Narrated to us Abu Salamah, informed to us Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muhammad, from Amr, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two things the son of Adam dislikes: death, and death is better for the believer than trial. And he dislikes little wealth, and little wealth is less for reckoning."
"24025","Narrated to us Sulayman ibn Dawud, informed to us Ismail, informed to me Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Asim, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned the like of it."
"24026","Narrated to us"
"24027","Narrated to us Abu Salamah, informed to us Abd al-Aziz, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Asim ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, protects His believing servant in the world while He loves him, as you protect your sick from food and drink, fearing for him."
"24028","Narrated to us Ibn Abi Adi, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, narrated to me Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Banu Abd al-Ashhal and prayed Maghrib with them. When he finished he said: Pray these two rakahs in your houses. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I said to my father: A man said: Whoever prays two rakahs after Maghrib in the mosque, it does not suffice him unless he prays them in his house, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is among the house prayers. He said: Who said this? I said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman. He said: How good what he said, or: how good what he derived."
"24029","Narrated to us Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ghasil, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, he said: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died. So they said: The sun eclipsed for the death of Ibrahim. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Indeed, they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life. So when you see them thus, rush to the mosques. Then he stood and recited, in what we think, part of Alif-Lam-Ra, a Book. Then he bowed, then he stood straight, then he prostrated two prostrations. Then he stood and did like what he did in the first."
"24030","Narrated to us Yunus, narrated to us Layth, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Amr, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most fearful of what I fear for you is minor shirk. They said: And what is minor shirk, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Showing off. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say to them on the Day of Resurrection, when people are recompensed for their deeds: Go to those you used to show off to in the world, and see whether you find any recompense with them."
"24031","Narrated to us Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Asim ibn Umar al-Zafari, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most fearful of what I fear for you. And he mentioned its meaning."
"24032","Narrated to us Yunus, narrated to us Layth, from Yazid, from Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, protects His servant from the world while He loves him, as you protect your sick from food and drink, fearing for him."
"24033","Narrated to us Yunus, narrated to us Layth, from Yazid, from Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah loves a people, He tries them. So whoever is patient, for him is patience, and whoever panics, for him is panic."
"24034","Narrated to us Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us my father, from Ibn Ishaq, narrated to me al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Saad ibn Muadh, brother of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, from Abu Sufyan, freedman of Ibn Abi Ahmad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: He used to say: Tell me of a man who entered Paradise and never prayed at all. When the people did not know him, they would ask him: Who is he? So he would say: Usayrim of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, Amr ibn Thabit ibn Waqsh. Al-Husayn said: So I said to Mahmud ibn Labid: How was the affair of al-Usayrim? He said: He used to refuse Islam against his people. When it was the day of Uhud, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Uhud, Islam occurred to him, so he accepted Islam. So he took his sword and went in the morning until he came to the people, and entered among the people, and fought until wounds incapacitated him. He said: While men of Banu Abd al-Ashhal were seeking their slain in the battle, they found him. So they said: By Allah, this is al-Usayrim. What has come? We left him while he denied this hadith. So they asked him: What brought you? They said: What brought you, O Amr? War against your people, or desire for Islam? He said: Rather desire for Islam. I believed in Allah and His Messenger, and I submitted. Then I took my sword and went in the morning with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I fought until what befell me befell me. He said: Then he did not remain long before he died in their hands. So they mentioned him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: He is among the people of Paradise."
"24035","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Isa, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Mahmud ibn Labid al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray Fajr in brightness, for it is greater for reward."
"24036","Abdullah said: I found this hadith in the book of my father in his handwriting: narrated to us Ishaq ibn Isa, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most fearful of what I fear for you is minor shirk. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is minor shirk? He said: Showing off. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say on the day the servants are recompensed for their deeds: Go to those you used to show off to with your deeds in the world, and see whether you find any recompense with them."
